          %p
            This is the motivation for the terminology “categories”, as the examples in Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfConcreteCategories"}
            are literally
            = succeed "." do
              %em categories of mathematical structures
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete
          %p Some terminology:
          #CommutingDiagram.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"}> commuting diagram
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
              labeled by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of the category is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              if for any two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
              any two ways of passing along edges from one to the other yields the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %p
              For example, a
              %em commuting triangle
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAAA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %mi h
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f = h \circ g
                    \\phantom{AAAAAA}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{ g }}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{ \mathrlap{ f } }
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;&amp; \underset{\phantom{A}h\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}  &amp;&amp; Z
                    }
            %p
              while a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAAA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 2
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_1 \circ f_1
                    \\;=\;
                    g_2 \circ f_2
                    \\phantom{AAAAAA}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\overset{\phantom{A}f_1\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_1
                    \\\
                    {}^{ \mathllap{f_2} }\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow^{\mathrlap{ g_1 }}
                    \\\
                    Y_2 &amp;\underset{\phantom{A}g_2\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;  Z
                    }
          #InitialObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \in \mathcal{C}
                  is called a
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  if for every other
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∃
                            %mo !
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        c \overset{\exists!}{\longrightarrow} \ast
                %p
                  hence if the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \in Set
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(c,\ast) \;\simeq\; \ast
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \in \mathcal{C}
                  is called an
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  if for every other
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∃
                            %mo !
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\emptyset \overset{\exists!}{\longrightarrow} c
                %p
                  hence if the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \in Set
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(\emptyset,c) \;\simeq\; \ast
                        \\,.
          #SmallCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"}> small category
                )
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Obj
                      %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              an actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              (i.e. a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              instead of a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
          %p As usual, there are some trivial examples, that are however usefully made explicit for the development of the theory:
          #InitialCategoryAndTerminalCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+category"} initial category
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  on this object, necessarily the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+category"} initial category
                  or
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+category"} empty category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  is the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            %p
              Clearly, these are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallCategory"}
          #PartiallyOrderedSetsAsSmallCategories.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preordered+sets"} preordered sets
                as
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+categories"} thin categories
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \leq)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preordered+set"} preordered set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to y
              whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
            #eq:RelationsAsMorphismInPartiallyOrderedSet.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mo !
                    %mi y
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mtext precisely if
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \overset{\exists !}{\to} y
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\text{precisely if}
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    x \leq y
            %p
              Conversely, every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              with at most one morphism from any object to any other, called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of a
