          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              That a hom-isomorphism
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} (10)
              implies units/counits satisfying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              is the statement of the second two items of Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAdjunctsInTermsOfAdjunctionUnitCounit"}
            %p
              Hence it remains to show the converse. But the argument is along the same lines as the proof of Prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAdjunctsInTermsOfAdjunctionUnitCounit"}
              %em define
              forming of adjuncts by the formula
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AdjunctFormula"} (16)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \mapsto \widetilde f
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              follows from the computation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
